# Database and security

- Active migrations are the five files in `supabase/migrations/`. Do not replay `supabase/legacy-migrations/`.
- Follow `CLAUDE.md`: cite sources, prove CHECK constraints, record row counts, UPSERT catalogue data, and write an idempotent SQL file after any MCP migration.
- Inspect columns and constraints before writing an import. Do not guess allowed values.
- Stop if remote migration history does not match the five-file baseline. Do not drop tables or reset the remote database.
- Protected routes must fail closed when Supabase auth cannot be evaluated.
- Authorise on the server. Do not trust client-supplied user ids. Do not use `user_metadata` for authorisation.
- Service-role access stays on the server. Never expose it to the browser.
- Webhook handlers must verify signatures. Do not log secrets or full payment payloads.
